========================================================================
jet stats --help
========================================================================
Usage: jet stats [options]

Shows channel profitability stats.

Options:
  --days <days>    Depth of history in days; max of 30 days, default 7
  --hours <hours>  Depth of history in hours; max of 720 hours, default 168
  --quiet          Quiet mode - only displays warn and error messages
  --verbose        Verbose mode - will also output debug messages
  --no-color       Disable colors
  -h, --help       display help for command

========================================================================
jet probes --help
========================================================================
Usage: jet probes [options]

Displays nodes discovered during probes that have signaled a commitment to
liquidity. This tool can be used to identify prospects for new channels.

Options:
  --days <days>    Depth of history in days
  --hours <hours>  Depth of history in hours
  --top <n>        Return top n records, default 10
  --all            Return all records
  --peers          Shows probe data for current peers instead of prospects for
                   new channels
  --sort <col>     Sort by a column (choices: "sats_sum", "count", "avg_ppm",
                   "min_ppm", "max_ppm")
  --quiet          Quiet mode - only displays warn and error messages
  --verbose        Verbose mode - will also output debug messages
  --no-color       Disable colors
  -h, --help       display help for command

========================================================================
jet rebalance --help
========================================================================
Usage: jet rebalance [options] <from> <to> <amount>

Rebalances the node via circular rebalance. Calls the BalanceOfSatoshis
rebalance API in a loop until the target amount is met or all possible routes
are exhausted.

Arguments:
  from           From this peer. Can be a partial alias, a pub id, or a BOS tag
  to             To this peer. Can be a partial alias, a pub id, or a BOS tag
  amount         Amount in sats

Options:
  --ppm <ppm>    Max ppm
  --mins <mins>  Max time to run in minutes
  --quiet        Quiet mode - only displays warn and error messages
  --verbose      Verbose mode - will also output debug messages
  --no-color     Disable colors
  -h, --help     display help for command

========================================================================
jet pay --help
========================================================================
Usage: jet pay [options] <request>

Pay a Lightning invoice.

Arguments:
  request              Payment Request

Options:
  --avoid <avoid>      Avoid forwarding via node/chan/tag (repeat for more)
  --in <peer>          Route through specific peer of destination
  --max-fee <sats>     Maximum fee to pay (default: 1337)
  --max-paths <paths>  Maximum paths to use (default: 1)
  --message <message>  Attach text message to payment
  --no-color           Mute all colors
  --node <node>        Node to use to pay payment request
  --out <peer>         Make first hop through peer (repeat for more)
  --quiet              Quiet mode - only displays warn and error messages
  --verbose            Verbose mode - will also output debug messages
  -h, --help           display help for command

========================================================================
jet peers --help
========================================================================
Usage: jet peers [options]

Lists peers classified into inbound, outbound and balanced based on routing
history.

Options:
  --days <days>  Depth of routing history in days (default: 1)
  --quiet        Quiet mode - only displays warn and error messages
  --verbose      Verbose mode - will also output debug messages
  --no-color     Disable colors
  -h, --help     display help for command

Notable columns:
  p       % of inbound or outbound routing by the peer out of total inbound or outbound across all peers
  ppm     peer's current ppm rate
  margin  rebalance ppm margin; rebalance will be profitable as long as its ppm is below this margin


