Lists peer fees.

Options:
  --quiet     Quiet mode - only displays warn and error messages
  --verbose   Verbose mode - will also output debug messages
  --no-color  Disable colors
  -h, --help  display help for command

========================================================================
jet analyze-fees --help
========================================================================
Usage: jet analyze-fees [options] [node]

Each peer's channel local and remote fees will be evaluated against the
profitability margin.

Arguments:
  node               Pub id or an alias, full or partial, of outbound node for
                     fee analysis

Options:
  --profit <profit>  Profit margin in % to evaluate fees against
  --quiet            Quiet mode - only displays warn and error messages
  --verbose          Verbose mode - will also output debug messages
  --no-color         Disable colors
  -h, --help         display help for command

========================================================================
jet htlc-history --help
========================================================================
Usage: jet htlc-history [options] [days]

Prints cumulative HTLC history for peers.

Arguments:
  days        Depth of history in days (default: 7)

Options:
  --quiet     Quiet mode - only displays warn and error messages
  --verbose   Verbose mode - will also output debug messages
  --no-color  Disable colors
  -h, --help  display help for command

Details:
  Prints % of total inbound / outbound routing for each peer.
  Example: inbound routing from a peer takes 25% of total inbound traffic across all peers.

  Also prints % of inbound / outbound routing for a peer.
  Example: inbound routing from a peer takes 95% of total routing from that peer.


========================================================================
jet htlc-analyzer --help
========================================================================
Usage: jet htlc-analyzer [options] [node]

Prints stats about failed HTLCs.

Arguments:
  node             Pub id or an alias, full or partial, of outbound node for
                   HTLC analysis

Options:
  --days <days>    Depth of history in days. Can provide partial days, e.g. .5
                   days for 12 hours
  --hours <hours>  Depth of history in hours
  --quiet          Quiet mode - only displays warn and error messages
  --verbose        Verbose mode - will also output debug messages
  --no-color       Disable colors
  -h, --help       display help for command

